exports[`APPSET phone golden (iOS 390, text) /notifications-settings reads exactly as recorded 1`] = `
"Stay in the Loop
Push lands on your phone right away; email is the lasting record when push misses. Turn either off per category. Both are on by default.
AI Morning Digest
A 6 AM brief of today's tasks, yesterday's field notes, weather risks, and what needs you. Pulled fresh each morning from your projects.
Send Me a Daily Brief
Couldn’t load your company profile. Tap the switch to retry.
Friday Close Nudge
A Friday 3 PM reminder to bill, chase, and close the week.
Friday 3 PM close nudge
On · Fridays at 3:00 PM local time
What MAGE Does on Its Own
Each ability is earned from your graded record and turns off when the record slips. Nothing is sent without you.
Pre-Set Durations from Your Pace
On. Draft schedules arrive with qualified trades already set to your measured pace (tap any badge to revert).
No graded pace calls yet. Apply "Your pace" suggestions on draft schedules and finish those tasks. Each graded call builds the record. A trade qualifies at 60% beat-or-tie over 5 calls.
Draft Change Orders from Leak Scans
On. Priced leaks in daily reports become draft COs for your review (drafts only, never sent).
No graded leak scans yet. Scan daily reports for leaks, then bill (or dismiss) the flagged items. Drafting qualifies at 50% billed over 5 scans.
From Your Website
When someone asks for a price on your website.
Category
Push
Email
Website Leads
Someone asks for a price through your website quote form or Instant Estimate widget.
From Your Client
When the client does something on the portal.
Category
Push
Email
Client Messages
Your client sends a message from the portal.
Contract Signed
Your client counter-signs the construction agreement.
Selection Picked
Your client picks a tile, fixture, or other allowance option.
Budget Proposals
Your client proposes a target budget from the portal.
CO Approvals
Your client approves or declines a change order.
Client Payments
Your client pays an invoice through the portal, or a bank payment fails after checkout.
From Your Team
When your field crew or a design pro sends something back.
Category
Push
Email
Field Daily Reports
Someone on your team files a daily report on one of your projects.
RFI and Submittal Responses
An architect, engineer, or reviewer answers an RFI or submittal you sent.
Incident Reports
Someone you invited files an incident report on one of your projects.
From Your Subs
When a sub does something through a link you sent them.
Category
Push
Email
Sub Invoices
A subcontractor submits an invoice through their portal.
Punch Items Ready
A subcontractor marks a punch item ready for your review.
Sub Bids Received
A subcontractor files a bid through an invite link you sent.
Lien Waiver Signed
A subcontractor signs a lien waiver you requested.
Prequalification Submitted
A subcontractor submits the prequalification packet you sent them.
Marketplace
New RFPs nearby, awards, and pre-bid Q&A.
Category
Push
Email
New Nearby RFPs
A client posts a project in your service area. These start once service-area setup is available, which it isn't yet.
Pre-Bid Questions
A contractor asks a question on an RFP you posted.
RFP Awarded to You
A client picks your bid for their project.
How Push Works
Your iPhone registers when you sign in. If you miss notifications, sign out and back in to register it again. Push isn't supported on the web app, but every category still sends emails there."
